Title:
GenAI Red Teaming Training

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4–8 sentences max):
- A self-paced curriculum and lab repository for offensive security testing of GenAI/LLM and broader AI/ML systems.  
- It aims to teach practical attacker techniques (beyond “Responsible AI” checks) to identify exploitable weaknesses such as prompt injection, data leakage, evasion, and poisoning.  
- The modules progress from foundations through prompt injection/jailbreaking, adversarial examples (white/black box), privacy attacks (membership inference/model inversion), poisoning/backdoors, and advanced LLM attacks (e.g., weight extraction, distillation, serialization issues).  
- It includes hands-on Jupyter notebooks and theory docs, plus an instructor guide and answer notebooks for exercises.  
- Uses common adversarial ML tooling (IBM ART, TextAttack, SHAP) and references OWASP LLM Top 10, NIST AI RMF, and MITRE ATLAS.  
- Most useful for red teamers, pentesters, and security researchers building AI security assessment capability; also relevant to blue teams designing test plans and regression suites for LLM/agent workflows.

Technical Focus:
- Prompt injection, jailbreaking, and guardrail bypass
- Adversarial example generation (white-box/black-box evasion)
- Privacy attacks: membership inference, model inversion, training data inference
- Data poisoning, backdoors, and AI supply-chain risk
- LLM-specific attacks: weight extraction, distillation, serialization vulnerabilities
- Agent security: planner/executor/reviewer threat modeling, sub-agent attacks, tool policy enforcement

Use Cases:
- Build and run an internal GenAI red teaming training program with labs and grading rubrics
- Develop repeatable security assessment playbooks aligned to OWASP LLM Top 10 / MITRE ATLAS
- Test LLM applications for prompt injection, tool misuse, and agent workflow weaknesses
- Evaluate model robustness against evasion/adversarial NLP attacks using ART/TextAttack
- Validate privacy posture (memorization/leakage) via membership inference and inversion exercises
- Create security regression tests for agentic systems and tool-calling policies

Keywords:
GenAI, LLM security, red teaming, prompt injection, jailbreaking, adversarial examples, evasion attacks, black-box attacks, white-box attacks, membership inference, model inversion, training data extraction, data poisoning, backdoor attacks, supply chain, serialization vulnerabilities, model weight extraction, model distillation, agent security, tool policy enforcement, OWASP LLM Top 10, NIST AI RMF, MITRE ATLAS, IBM ART, TextAttack, SHAP, Jupyter notebooks, Python 3.12, transformers, torch